From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:28:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: test switch for a gap before the
 reference area

On the J604 a 4K 10-bit HEVC frame decodes 0.42 ms slower than an 8-bit
one when the decoder writes 16-bit samples, and at full speed (699 fps,
macOS's rate) in its packed 10-bit mode, which writes a third fewer
bytes. macOS writes the same 16-bit picture at full speed, with no GPU
or CPU help, into a surface that holds only the picture.

Each CAPTURE buffer here holds the picture and, right behind it, the
compressed reference copy the decoder writes at the same time. Both are
written in 32-row bands of the same size, so the two write streams stay
exactly one picture apart for the whole frame.

Add comp_gap_kib, a test-only parameter (default 0, no change) that puts
that many KiB between the two, so that the decode rate can be measured
against the distance.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c
index 0b6df1c44b..745b23fa23 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-v4l2.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
  * Copyright (C) 2011 Samsung Electronics Co., Ltd.
  */
 
+#include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 
 #include <media/v4l2-event.h>
@@ -103,13 +104,31 @@ static bool avd_is_valid_fmt(struct avd_ctx *ctx, u32 fourcc,
 	return false;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Test switch (default 0): KiB of space between the picture and the
+ * compressed reference area after it in each CAPTURE buffer. The decoder
+ * writes both in 32-row bands of the same size, so without a gap the two
+ * streams of writes stay a fixed picture size apart for the whole frame.
+ * Read when the CAPTURE format is set, so it applies to the next stream.
+ */
+static unsigned int comp_gap_kib;
+module_param(comp_gap_kib, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(comp_gap_kib,
+		 "Test only: KiB between the picture and its compressed reference area (default 0)");
+
 static void avd_fill_decoded_pixfmt(struct avd_ctx *ctx,
 				    struct v4l2_pix_format_mplane *pix_mp)
 {
+	unsigned int gap = min(READ_ONCE(comp_gap_kib), 65536U);
+
 	v4l2_fill_pixfmt_mp(pix_mp, pix_mp->pixelformat, pix_mp->width,
 			    pix_mp->height);
 
 	ctx->comp.start_offset = pix_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage;
+	if (gap)
+		ctx->comp.start_offset = ALIGN(ctx->comp.start_offset, SZ_4K) +
+					 (size_t)gap * SZ_1K;
+	pix_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = ctx->comp.start_offset;
 	fill_comp(&ctx->comp, ctx->image_fmt, pix_mp->width, pix_mp->height);
 	pix_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage += ctx->comp.size;
 	if (ctx->coded_fmt_desc->ops->adjust_decoded_fmt)
-- 
